  {
   "role": "system",
   "content": "You are SCOUT. You have candidate papers found by literature search for a paper under review.\nSelect the papers most useful for VERIFYING the listed claims: direct prior work the paper compares against, work that reports competing numbers on the same benchmarks, and follow-up work that confirms or challenges the claims.\n\nRules:\n- Return up to 3 candidate keys (e.g. P3) in `selected`, most relevant first.\n- Ignore papers that are only topically similar but cannot confirm or refute any claim.\n- Never select the paper under review itself.\n- Put a short `reasoning` first."
  },
  {
   "role": "user",
   "content": "Paper under review: GatedMix: Gated Token Mixing for Translation\n\nClaims to verify:\nC1: GatedMix reaches 27.1 BLEU on WMT 2014 English-German, outperforming all previous single models, while training 3x faster than an LSTM baseline.\nC2: To our knowledge, GatedMix is the first model to use gated token mixing for translation.\n\nCandidates (key | year | title | abstract excerpt):\nP1 | 2017 | Convolutional Sequence to Sequence Learning | We introduce an architecture based entirely on convolutional neural networks. ConvS2S reaches 26.4 BLEU on WMT 2014 English-German and outperforms the LSTM setup of Wu et al. (2016) on WMT'14 English-French, while being an order of magnitude faster on GPU.\nP2 | 2016 | Gated Token Mixers for Language Modeling | We propose gated token mixers, a layer that relates all positions of a sequence through a learned gate. Applied to language modeling and to machine translation, gated token mixers match LSTM quality while training twice as fast.\nP3 | 2017 | A Strong Attention Baseline for Translation | Our attention-only model obtains 28.4 BLEU on WMT 2014 English-German as a single model, establishing a new state of the art.\n\nSelect up to 3 keys via the `submit_selection` tool."
  }
